WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.080
Which melts ice faster:

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.220
room-temperature
metal or wood?

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.820
Metal feels colder—but
its ice can melt faster.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.020
Why? Your hand is warmer
than both materials.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.840
Metal carries heat away
from your skin quickly,

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.340
so it feels cold.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.240
Ice is colder than both.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.140
Now metal transfers
heat toward the ice.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.990
Same material.
Opposite direction.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.940
Ordinary has secrets.
